# CTRLO-OTHER-PICKERS round 3: the settings menu with a search typed, then
# Ctrl-O and an edit key in one burst (`key -H`, one send-keys), as
# p5-ctrlo-burst-help over the catalog.
# `e`, C-a, `s`: the search `se`, the caret between its two letters; Down
# twice moves the mark (`typed`).
# Ctrl-O and C-j: the composer's line break inside the word, no menu synced
# (insert_newline, app_input_runtime.zig:513-521@481104fd), so the mark
# stays on its index (`burst-cj`).
# Ctrl-O and C-k: a kill of the `e` after the caret, which syncs the menu
# (delete_to_line_end, app_input_runtime.zig:479-488, :485): the mark is
# back on the first row (`burst-ck`).
# fx's harness launches it with FX_SOUND=0; xfx is given the same start.
fx: env FX_AUTO_UPGRADE=0
xfx: env XFX_SOUND=off
wait 2
type /settings
key Enter
wait 1
type e
key C-a
type s
wait 0.4
key Down
wait 0.3
key Down
wait 0.5
snap typed
key -H 0f 0a
wait 0.8
snap burst-cj
key -H 0f 0b
wait 0.8
snap burst-ck
